From: nxrs contributors
Subject: [PATCH] pynuttx: restore task inspection state and read native owners

The pinned mutex holder moved into sem.val.mholder. Decode that native
representation, including the waiter bit and no-owner/reset sentinels.
Report the ps command's -g3 requirement explicitly when macro data is absent.

Use the connected ARM register description. Xtensa's native offset table
uses a canonical order and includes reserved slots: it does not match the
Espressif remote packet, and regs_num is not its array length. Load logical
a0..a15 from the complete native table, retain the live window base, and
unwind prior spilled windows only after installing the full saved context.

Task apply commands use the running task's live context and restore the
original physical register bank, thread, and selected frame in finally,
including when the inspection command raises. Snapshot register integers
before changing context. No target firmware code or debugger target calls
are added.

